---
import PlatformLayout from '../../layouts/PlatformLayout.astro';
import SettingCard from '../../components/SettingCard.astro';
import WarningCallout from '../../components/WarningCallout.astro';
import CrossLinkChip from '../../components/CrossLinkChip.astro';
import FactCard from '../../components/FactCard.astro';
import platformData from '../../data/platforms/youtube.json';
---

<PlatformLayout
  title="YouTube"
  description="YouTube builds a detailed behavioral profile from every video you watch, including the ones you never finish. Here are the settings that matter and what they actually do."
  subtitle=""
  category="Video Platform"
  lastVerified="March 23, 2026"
  settingsCount={platformData.settings.length}
  severity="high"
  severityText="YouTube is a Google product. Most privacy settings are located in Google Account (myaccount.google.com) rather than YouTube itself. Watch history, search history, and engagement patterns feed Google's advertising network, one of the largest in the world. YouTube's recommendation algorithm is trained on granular viewing behavior including pause points, rewind patterns, and skip decisions."
  owner="Alphabet Inc. (Google)"
  ownerHQ="Mountain View, CA"
  headquarters="San Bruno, CA"
  monthlyUsers="~2.7B MAU"
  relatedPractices={[
    { label: 'Off-Platform Activity Tracking', href: '/practices/off-platform-tracking' },
    { label: 'Ad Personalization & Targeting', href: '/practices/ad-personalization' },
    { label: 'AI Training Data Usage', href: '/practices/ai-training' },
    { label: 'Third-Party Data Sharing', href: '/practices/third-party-sharing' },
  ]}
>

  <!-- WHAT THEY COLLECT -->
  <div slot="what-they-collect">
    <div class="fact-grid">
      <FactCard
        label="Every video you watch, and how you watch it"
        text="YouTube logs which videos you play, at what time, from what device, how far through each video you watched, where you paused, what you rewound, and what you skipped. This granular engagement data trains the recommendation algorithm and informs ad targeting."
        severity="critical"
      />
      <FactCard
        label="Every search query on YouTube"
        text="YouTube Search history is stored separately from Google Search history. Every query entered into YouTube is logged and associated with your account or device."
        severity="high"
      />
      <FactCard
        label="Your YouTube activity informs ads across Google"
        text="YouTube watch history and search behavior feed into the same Google advertising profile used for ads in Search, Gmail, Maps, and across the Google Display Network. YouTube is not a separate data silo."
        severity="high"
      />
      <FactCard
        label="Inferred beliefs and health from viewing patterns"
        text="YouTube knows which political channels, health topics, religious content, and news sources you watch. These signals are used to infer demographic attributes and interests for ad targeting."
        severity="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="collect-detail">
      <p>YouTube is a Google product, and its data flows into Google's unified advertising profile. There is no meaningful separation between your YouTube data and your Google data. Watching YouTube while logged into a Google Account adds to the same behavioral profile that governs ads you see on Google Search, in Gmail, and across the Display Network.</p>

      <p>YouTube collects more granular viewing behavior than most users realize. Not just which videos you watched, but your engagement pattern within each video. Whether you skipped the first 30 seconds. Whether you rewound a segment. Whether you watched a video to completion or abandoned it at 40%. This behavioral signal is the core input for the recommendation algorithm.</p>

      <p>Viewing history also creates inferences. A user who consistently watches videos from certain political channels, certain religious content creators, or certain health-focused channels has those interests and beliefs inferred and added to their advertising profile.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SETTINGS THAT MATTER -->
  <div slot="settings">
    {(() => {
      let lastSeverity = null;
      return platformData.settings.map((s) => {
        const showLabel = s.severity !== "critical" && s.severity !== lastSeverity;
        lastSeverity = s.severity;
        return (
          <>
            {showLabel && <h3 class="severity-group-label">{s.severity.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.severity.slice(1)}</h3>}
            <SettingCard
              name={s.name}
              severity={s.severity}
              defaultState={s.defaultState}
              platform={s.platform}
              path={s.path}
              webUrl={s.webUrl ?? undefined}
              webPath={s.webPath ?? undefined}
              description={s.description}
              whatItDoesnt={s.whatItDoesnt}
            />
          </>
        );
      });
    })()}
  </div>


    <div class="turnoff-group">
      <h3 class="turnoff-heading">Ad Personalization</h3>
      <ol class="turnoff-steps">
        <li>myaccount.google.com &rarr; Data &amp; privacy &rarr; Ad settings &rarr; Ad personalization.</li>
        <li>Toggle off "Ad personalization is ON."</li>
        <li>This applies across all Google products including YouTube, Search, and Gmail.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="turnoff-group">
      <h3 class="turnoff-heading">Web & App Activity (Cross-Product Sharing)</h3>
      <ol class="turnoff-steps">
        <li>myaccount.google.com &rarr; Data &amp; privacy &rarr; Web &amp; App Activity.</li>
        <li>Click "Turn off" to stop YouTube activity from being shared across Google products.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="turnoff-group">
      <h3 class="turnoff-heading">Location Permissions</h3>
      <ol class="turnoff-steps">
        <li>On iPhone: Settings &rarr; YouTube &rarr; Location &rarr; set to Never.</li>
        <li>On Android: Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; YouTube &rarr; Permissions &rarr; Location &rarr; Deny.</li>
        <li>IP-based location inference cannot be blocked at the app level.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="turnoff-group">
      <h3 class="turnoff-heading">Connected Third-Party Apps</h3>
      <ol class="turnoff-steps">
        <li>myaccount.google.com &rarr; Security &rarr; Third-party apps with account access.</li>
        <li>Review apps with YouTube access and remove any you no longer use.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- WHO GETS YOUR DATA -->
  <div slot="who-gets-data">
    <dl class="data-recipients">
      <div class="recipient">
        <dt>Google's Advertising Network</dt>
        <dd>YouTube behavioral data feeds into Google's advertising profile and is used to target ads on YouTube, Google Search, Gmail, Maps, and millions of third-party websites in the Google Display Network.</dd>
      </div>

      <div class="recipient">
        <dt>Display & Video 360</dt>
        <dd>Google's enterprise advertising platform for agencies and major brands. YouTube viewership data informs audience segments available to advertisers running campaigns through DV360.</dd>
      </div>

      <div class="recipient">
        <dt>YouTube Content Partners</dt>
        <dd>YouTube channel owners and multi-channel networks receive analytics about their audience, including demographic breakdowns and engagement metrics. Individual viewer data is not shared, but aggregate signals are.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <!-- WHAT THEY KNOW -->
  <div slot="what-they-know">
    <p>A year of YouTube watch history is readable as a biography. The algorithm infers: political leanings (from news and commentary content), religious affiliation or interest, health concerns (from medical content), relationship status and family composition (from wedding content, parenting content), profession and industry (from professional learning content), and approximate age (from content era preferences). These inferences are not disclosed to you but are used as targeting parameters available to any advertiser running campaigns through Google's ad platform.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- RELATED PRACTICES -->
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-practices" href="/practices/off-platform-tracking" label="Off-Platform Activity Tracking" type="practice" />
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-practices" href="/practices/ad-personalization" label="Ad Personalization" type="practice" />
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-practices" href="/practices/ai-training" label="AI Training Data Usage" type="practice" />
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-practices" href="/practices/location-data" label="Location Data" type="practice" />
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-practices" href="/rights/coppa" label="COPPA ($170M fine, YouTube Kids)" type="practice" />

  <!-- RELATED PLATFORMS -->
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-platforms" href="/platforms/google" label="Google" type="platform" />
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-platforms" href="/platforms/meta" label="Meta / Instagram" type="platform" />
  <CrossLinkChip slot="related-platforms" href="/platforms/tiktok" label="TikTok" type="platform" />

</PlatformLayout>

<style>
  .fact-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .collect-detail {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .severity-group-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.375rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .severity-group-label:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .turnoff-group {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .turnoff-group:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .turnoff-heading {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .turnoff-steps {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.375rem;
  }

  .turnoff-steps li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .data-recipients {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .recipient {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .recipient:first-child {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .recipient:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .recipient dt {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }

  .recipient dd {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
